# GLM-5.2 MoE GEMM kernel work — always reference

Full working notes: `results/glm52_prefill_i1k_c64_profile.md` (the `MoE gemm1`/`gemm2` detail
sections + the status/levers table). Read it before touching a kernel.

## Current focus: gemm1 (gate-up) new-CK small-M loss — the REAL fix

- New-CK `gufusion_v3` (gate-up fusion) gemm1 vs FlyDSL `mfma_moe1 t128x128x256`, prod shape
  (6144,512 per-rank, a4w4), per-call µs: **wins M≥8192 (−5→−7.6%), loses M≤4096**
  (1024 +35%, 4096 +12%; 8192 −5.0%, 16384 −7.6%, 32768 −7.3%). Numerically ==FlyDSL
  (logits_diff 1e-5).
- **Goal: root-cause and fix the small-M regression** so CK wins across all M. That makes CK
  viable for BOTH stages (gemm2 is already at parity) and removes the need for the fragile
  CK-gemm1 ↔ FlyDSL-gemm2 "mixed dispatch" — that handoff (different intermediate layout/sort
  contracts, breaks at some M) is a band-aid, not a solution.
- CK gemm1 target: `csrc/ck_tile_gemm_moe_2stages/` (kernel `moe_cktile2stages.cu` /
  `include/moe_cktile2stages_common.cuh`; per-shape codegen `gen_instances.py`).

## gemm2 (down-GEMM): PARKED — do NOT rewrite

- CK port (`flydsl_mxmoe_g2` / `mfma_moe2`) ≈ FlyDSL at best (−1% @16k, +15% @8k); the newer CK
  version is ~39% slower @16k. No CK win. The 0.55x vs B200 gap is architectural (FlyDSL-vs-B200),
  not closeable by a CK rewrite.
- The glm5-shape codegen gap (`(257,6144,512,9)` missing from `csrc/kernels/mxfp4_moe/moe_aux/codegen/gen_instances.py SHAPES`)
  is only WHY it defaults to FlyDSL — closing it yields no perf. FlyDSL gemm2 lives in
  `aiter/ops/flydsl/kernels/mixed_moe_gemm_2stage.py` (`compile_mixed_moe_gemm2`); leave it alone.
- Disregard all legacy `kernel_moe_mxgemm_2lds` bypass numbers (2.4×/2855us/occupancy/split-K) —
  that path was never deployed.

## Non-negotiable gotchas (each burned real cycles)

1. After ANY FlyDSL kernel edit: `rm -rf /sgl-workspace/aiter-gemm1/aiter/jit/flydsl_cache/*` before
   testing — the FlyDSL disk cache silently serves the OLD kernel otherwise. (CK edits: rebuild the
   affected module; confirm recompile with a `sys.stderr.write` in the compile/gen path.)
2. `logits_diff` varies run-to-run (random fp4 inputs) — NOT a valid before/after delta. Judge perf
   by rocprof `MfmaUtil` / per-call µs.
3. rocprofv3 multi-metric `--pmc A B C` HANGS — use single-metric passes + `--kernel-trace`; analyze
   with `utilities/pmc_pick.py` / `utilities/kt_analyze.py`.

## Dev flow

Box `smci355-ccs-aus-m12-17.cs-aus.dcgpu`, container `macui-glm5`. Build and benchmark in
`/sgl-workspace/aiter-gemm1` (`PYTHONPATH=/sgl-workspace/aiter-gemm1`); leave `/sgl-workspace/aiter`
(stock, pip-editable) untouched. Local counterpart is `/home/macui/aiter-gemm1`, a worktree of
`/home/macui/aiter` on `RM/glm52-mxfp4-moe-ck-gemm1` with CK on `RM/glm52-a4w4-k256-swizzle-fix`.
Microbench (single GPU): `python3 op_tests/test_moe_2stage.py --kernel --no-legacy --csv-filter
moe_ck2stages` with `AITER_CONFIG_FMOE` pinning the arm; `-t <M>` selects the token count.
Adding a codegen instance requires deleting `aiter/jit/module_moe_ck2stages_*.so` **and** its
`aiter/jit/build/<same name>/` directory — `AITER_REBUILD=1` alone reuses the stale instance blob
and the run silently falls back with `ck kernel not found`.
Check `rocm-smi` for an idle GPU before microbenching; the box is shared.
